# INVOL option 7 on a DS5500: initialise the physical badspot list.
#
# `MD14`, not `MD7C` -- the banner's digits are the SAU number.
#
# `Use automated badspot entry? n` is C50's answer and its reason still holds:
# MAME's own driver notes list Winchester bad-track formatting as a known gap,
# so automated entry asks the emulated controller for the one thing its author
# does not vouch for. The medium is a file and cannot have defects, so the
# badspot list is terminated with a blank line.
expect MD14
expect >
send DI C\r
expect >
send EX INVOL\r
expect Option:
send 7\r
expect q=Quit
send w\r
expect automated badspot
send n\r
expect Terminate badspot entry
send \r
expect correct?
send y\r
expect Anything more to do
send n\r
